{"duration_api_ms":103015,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"4d1e7acc-bcab-4a49-adac-265402a32356","total_cost_usd":1.74834,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":67391,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":8010,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3783},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":67391,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8010,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":67391,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":67391},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":8010,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":67391,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.74834,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":3783,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":2,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"schema\":\"agent-ee.review/1\",\"candidate_id\":\"62f16f3261185780b238caa726245d57ddcd2230c124e5e360b89aef094fd927\",\"run_id\":\"4c35aac2-1907-4a00-b689-ae18e9cf2fe6\",\"packet_sha256\":\"94771d3fc05f4295e0a8f1af959918cf22251edb707b8a6118f0c43a6817dd92\",\"role\":\"circuit\",\"coverage\":[\"Checked ERC record (work/erc/erc.json, console.log): 0 violations on 1 sheet; ignored-check list reviewed and none of the ignored categories hide a connectivity-relevant issue for this 3-component design.\",\"Checked DRC record (work/drc/drc.json): 0 violations, 0 unconnected items, 0 schematic-parity issues on the saved board.\",\"Cross-checked netlist (work/netlist/design.xml, connectivity.json) against pad net assignments in inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb: /IN=J1.1+R1.1, /OUT=C1.1+J1.2+R1.2, GND=C1.2+J1.3 all match; schematic local labels IN/OUT and GND power symbols are consistent with the exported nets.\",\"Manually verified all five track segments in inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb are width 0.25 mm, meeting the declared 0.20 mm minimum; geometry probe output (work/geometry/geometry.json) agrees with the native board file.\",\"Traced the GND return path in the saved board: C1 pad 2 (110.95,100) F.Cu track to via (113,100), via to B.Cu zone, zone thermal relief to J1 pad 3 (100,105.08); the saved filled_polygon contains the via location and thermal spokes at pad 3.\",\"Independently recomputed the RC step response: tau = 100 kOhm x 100 nF = 10 ms; 1 - exp(-0.1) = 0.0951626 V at 1 ms and 1 - exp(-0.5) = 0.393469 V at 5 ms, matching ngspice measurements (work/rc-step/ngspice.log), confirming the simulation deck (work/rc-step/deck.cir) faithfully represents the saved R1=100k, C1=100n values and node mapping.\",\"Reviewed the ngspice deck and control script: PWL(0 0 1n 1) 1 V step, .tran 0.005m 5m, .meas at 1 ms and 5 ms; stimulus and measurement method are appropriate for the declared unloaded ideal step requirement; J1 exclusion from simulation is correct (connector, exclude_from_sim yes).\"],\"limitations\":[\"Binary waveform work/rc-step/result.raw was not readable by this text reviewer; conclusions rest on ngspice.log .meas values, which match the analytic solution exactly.\",\"The vout_5ms measurement carries no min/max limits in the criteria, so it constrains nothing; it served only as a secondary consistency point in this review.\",\"Zone fill was evaluated as saved (read-only candidate, no refill pass), per the packet's declared limitation.\",\"Per the declared scope, component tolerance, temperature, external loading, ADC sampling, EMI and physical hardware behavior are untested; no part ratings (R1 power, C1 voltage) were evaluated because no operating conditions beyond the 1 V ideal step are stated.\",\"Via size/drill and zone minimum thickness are outside the declared track-segment width requirement and were not judged against any limit.\"],\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"CKT-1\",\"title\":\"R1 = 100k (should be 10k): step response fails requirement 1 by an order of magnitude\",\"location\":\"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_sch, symbol R1 (uuid c5c38e1a-7593-5c99-b971-2f9d2e7bef78), property Value \\\"100k\\\"; same value on the board footprint R1 (inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb, uuid 8404a180-a151-464e-8f25-8cf316cdcba5)\",\"condition\":\"The declared requirement (inputs/requirements/fixture-requirements.md, item 1) specifies 0.62 V <= V(/OUT, 1 ms) <= 0.65 V for a 1 V ideal step, with intended R1 = 10 kohm, C1 = 100 nF, tau = 1 ms. The saved schematic and board populate R1 = 100 kohm.\",\"mechanism\":\"With R1 = 100 kohm and C1 = 100 nF, tau = R*C = 10 ms instead of 1 ms. At t = 1 ms the unloaded output is V = 1*(1 - exp(-0.1)) = 0.0951626 V, far below the 0.62 V lower limit. The ngspice transient measured vout_1ms = 0.09516251 V (work/rc-step/ngspice.log), matching the analytic value, and vout_5ms = 0.3934693 V matches 1 - exp(-0.5) = 0.3934693, confirming the deck (C1 OUT 0 100n; R1 IN OUT 100k) and node mapping are faithful to the saved design. The failure is therefore a component-value error in the design, not a simulation or tooling artifact.\",\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"assessment\":\"defect\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_sch\",\"locator\":\"symbol R1, property \\\"Value\\\" \\\"100k\\\" (uuid c5c38e1a-7593-5c99-b971-2f9d2e7bef78)\"},{\"path\":\"inputs/requirements/fixture-requirements.md\",\"locator\":\"item 1: 0.62 V <= V(/OUT, 1 ms) <= 0.65 V; intended R1 = 10 kohm, tau = 1 ms\"},{\"path\":\"work/rc-step/deck.cir\",\"locator\":\"lines: C1 OUT 0 100n / R1 IN OUT 100k / VSTEP IN 0 PWL(0 0 1n 1)\"},{\"path\":\"work/rc-step/ngspice.log\",\"locator\":\"Measurements: vout_1ms = 9.516251e-02, vout_5ms = 3.934693e-01\"},{\"path\":\"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb\",\"locator\":\"footprint Resistor_SMD:R_0805_2012Metric, property \\\"Value\\\" \\\"100k\\\" (uuid 8404a180-a151-464e-8f25-8cf316cdcba5)\"}],\"reasoning\":\"Independent calculation confirms the measurement: tau = 100e3 * 100e-9 = 10 ms, so V(1 ms) = 1 - exp(-0.1) = 0.0951626 V, agreeing with the simulated 0.09516251 V to 7 significant figures, and the unconstrained 5 ms point also matches theory exactly. The simulation model, stimulus (1 V PWL step with 1 ns rise, negligible at 1 ms) and .meas method are sound, so the limit violation is attributable solely to the populated R1 value being 10x the intended 10 kohm. This fails the fixture's primary declared acceptance criterion, so the design cannot pass as saved; the correction is R1 = 10k in both schematic and board.\"},{\"id\":\"CKT-2\",\"title\":\"Geometry probe emitted native KiCad assertion failures during the run\",\"location\":\"work/geometry/console.log\",\"condition\":\"The geometry probe's console log contains three repeated native assertion messages: './kicad/include/properties/property.h(607): assert \\\"m_choices.GetCount() > 0\\\" failed in PROPERTY_ENUM(): No enum choices defined', alongside the normal summary line 'geometry: 3 footprint(s), 6 track item(s), 1 zone(s)'.\",\"mechanism\":\"A native assertion inside the pcbnew Python bindings indicates the library hit an unexpected internal state while loading the board. The probe still exited 0 and produced complete output, but a successful exit is not by itself proof that the extracted geometry is complete; an assertion could in principle accompany skipped or misread objects.\",\"severity\":\"info\",\"assessment\":\"concern\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/geometry/console.log\",\"locator\":\"three 'assert \\\"m_choices.GetCount() > 0\\\" failed in PROPERTY_ENUM()' lines\"},{\"path\":\"work/geometry/geometry.json\",\"locator\":\"tracks array (5 segments, all width_mm 0.25) and pads array (7 pads), which match the native board file\"},{\"path\":\"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb\",\"locator\":\"five (segment ...) items, each (width 0.25); one (via ...); one (zone ...)\"}],\"reasoning\":\"I cross-checked the probe's JSON against the native board file by hand: all five segments, the via, the seven pads with their nets/positions, and the single B.Cu GND zone are present and correct, so the geometry pass verdict (narrowest 0.25 mm >= 0.20 mm required) stands. The assertions appear to be benign tool noise (likely a pcbnew property-registration quirk), but they are a native violation in the toolchain and worth tracking in case a future, larger board exercises the same code path with real consequences.\"}]}","structured_output":{"schema":"agent-ee.review/1","candidate_id":"62f16f3261185780b238caa726245d57ddcd2230c124e5e360b89aef094fd927","run_id":"4c35aac2-1907-4a00-b689-ae18e9cf2fe6","packet_sha256":"94771d3fc05f4295e0a8f1af959918cf22251edb707b8a6118f0c43a6817dd92","role":"circuit","coverage":["Checked ERC record (work/erc/erc.json, console.log): 0 violations on 1 sheet; ignored-check list reviewed and none of the ignored categories hide a connectivity-relevant issue for this 3-component design.","Checked DRC record (work/drc/drc.json): 0 violations, 0 unconnected items, 0 schematic-parity issues on the saved board.","Cross-checked netlist (work/netlist/design.xml, connectivity.json) against pad net assignments in inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb: /IN=J1.1+R1.1, /OUT=C1.1+J1.2+R1.2, GND=C1.2+J1.3 all match; schematic local labels IN/OUT and GND power symbols are consistent with the exported nets.","Manually verified all five track segments in inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb are width 0.25 mm, meeting the declared 0.20 mm minimum; geometry probe output (work/geometry/geometry.json) agrees with the native board file.","Traced the GND return path in the saved board: C1 pad 2 (110.95,100) F.Cu track to via (113,100), via to B.Cu zone, zone thermal relief to J1 pad 3 (100,105.08); the saved filled_polygon contains the via location and thermal spokes at pad 3.","Independently recomputed the RC step response: tau = 100 kOhm x 100 nF = 10 ms; 1 - exp(-0.1) = 0.0951626 V at 1 ms and 1 - exp(-0.5) = 0.393469 V at 5 ms, matching ngspice measurements (work/rc-step/ngspice.log), confirming the simulation deck (work/rc-step/deck.cir) faithfully represents the saved R1=100k, C1=100n values and node mapping.","Reviewed the ngspice deck and control script: PWL(0 0 1n 1) 1 V step, .tran 0.005m 5m, .meas at 1 ms and 5 ms; stimulus and measurement method are appropriate for the declared unloaded ideal step requirement; J1 exclusion from simulation is correct (connector, exclude_from_sim yes)."],"limitations":["Binary waveform work/rc-step/result.raw was not readable by this text reviewer; conclusions rest on ngspice.log .meas values, which match the analytic solution exactly.","The vout_5ms measurement carries no min/max limits in the criteria, so it constrains nothing; it served only as a secondary consistency point in this review.","Zone fill was evaluated as saved (read-only candidate, no refill pass), per the packet's declared limitation.","Per the declared scope, component tolerance, temperature, external loading, ADC sampling, EMI and physical hardware behavior are untested; no part ratings (R1 power, C1 voltage) were evaluated because no operating conditions beyond the 1 V ideal step are stated.","Via size/drill and zone minimum thickness are outside the declared track-segment width requirement and were not judged against any limit."],"findings":[{"id":"CKT-1","title":"R1 = 100k (should be 10k): step response fails requirement 1 by an order of magnitude","location":"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_sch, symbol R1 (uuid c5c38e1a-7593-5c99-b971-2f9d2e7bef78), property Value \"100k\"; same value on the board footprint R1 (inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb, uuid 8404a180-a151-464e-8f25-8cf316cdcba5)","condition":"The declared requirement (inputs/requirements/fixture-requirements.md, item 1) specifies 0.62 V <= V(/OUT, 1 ms) <= 0.65 V for a 1 V ideal step, with intended R1 = 10 kohm, C1 = 100 nF, tau = 1 ms. The saved schematic and board populate R1 = 100 kohm.","mechanism":"With R1 = 100 kohm and C1 = 100 nF, tau = R*C = 10 ms instead of 1 ms. At t = 1 ms the unloaded output is V = 1*(1 - exp(-0.1)) = 0.0951626 V, far below the 0.62 V lower limit. The ngspice transient measured vout_1ms = 0.09516251 V (work/rc-step/ngspice.log), matching the analytic value, and vout_5ms = 0.3934693 V matches 1 - exp(-0.5) = 0.3934693, confirming the deck (C1 OUT 0 100n; R1 IN OUT 100k) and node mapping are faithful to the saved design. The failure is therefore a component-value error in the design, not a simulation or tooling artifact.","severity":"blocking","assessment":"defect","evidence":[{"path":"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_sch","locator":"symbol R1, property \"Value\" \"100k\" (uuid c5c38e1a-7593-5c99-b971-2f9d2e7bef78)"},{"path":"inputs/requirements/fixture-requirements.md","locator":"item 1: 0.62 V <= V(/OUT, 1 ms) <= 0.65 V; intended R1 = 10 kohm, tau = 1 ms"},{"path":"work/rc-step/deck.cir","locator":"lines: C1 OUT 0 100n / R1 IN OUT 100k / VSTEP IN 0 PWL(0 0 1n 1)"},{"path":"work/rc-step/ngspice.log","locator":"Measurements: vout_1ms = 9.516251e-02, vout_5ms = 3.934693e-01"},{"path":"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb","locator":"footprint Resistor_SMD:R_0805_2012Metric, property \"Value\" \"100k\" (uuid 8404a180-a151-464e-8f25-8cf316cdcba5)"}],"reasoning":"Independent calculation confirms the measurement: tau = 100e3 * 100e-9 = 10 ms, so V(1 ms) = 1 - exp(-0.1) = 0.0951626 V, agreeing with the simulated 0.09516251 V to 7 significant figures, and the unconstrained 5 ms point also matches theory exactly. The simulation model, stimulus (1 V PWL step with 1 ns rise, negligible at 1 ms) and .meas method are sound, so the limit violation is attributable solely to the populated R1 value being 10x the intended 10 kohm. This fails the fixture's primary declared acceptance criterion, so the design cannot pass as saved; the correction is R1 = 10k in both schematic and board."},{"id":"CKT-2","title":"Geometry probe emitted native KiCad assertion failures during the run","location":"work/geometry/console.log","condition":"The geometry probe's console log contains three repeated native assertion messages: './kicad/include/properties/property.h(607): assert \"m_choices.GetCount() > 0\" failed in PROPERTY_ENUM(): No enum choices defined', alongside the normal summary line 'geometry: 3 footprint(s), 6 track item(s), 1 zone(s)'.","mechanism":"A native assertion inside the pcbnew Python bindings indicates the library hit an unexpected internal state while loading the board. The probe still exited 0 and produced complete output, but a successful exit is not by itself proof that the extracted geometry is complete; an assertion could in principle accompany skipped or misread objects.","severity":"info","assessment":"concern","evidence":[{"path":"work/geometry/console.log","locator":"three 'assert \"m_choices.GetCount() > 0\" failed in PROPERTY_ENUM()' lines"},{"path":"work/geometry/geometry.json","locator":"tracks array (5 segments, all width_mm 0.25) and pads array (7 pads), which match the native board file"},{"path":"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb","locator":"five (segment ...) items, each (width 0.25); one (via ...); one (zone ...)"}],"reasoning":"I cross-checked the probe's JSON against the native board file by hand: all five segments, the via, the seven pads with their nets/positions, and the single B.Cu GND zone are present and correct, so the geometry pass verdict (narrowest 0.25 mm >= 0.20 mm required) stands. The assertions appear to be benign tool noise (likely a pcbnew property-registration quirk), but they are a native violation in the toolchain and worth tracking in case a future, larger board exercises the same code path with real consequences."}]},"ttft_ms":53733,"type":"result","duration_ms":103311,"uuid":"ebcb9afa-0256-49b8-a9d6-28e9d5b6266c","ttft_stream_ms":2575,"time_to_request_ms":294,"first_content_frame_ms":2576,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
